{"translation":"Ascending the Heights

By Du Fu

The wind is swift, the sky is high; the gibbons' cries are sad,
The isle is clear, the sand is white; birds wheel in flight.
Boundless, the falling leaves descend, rustling down;
Endless, the Yangtze River rolls on, surging onward.
Ten thousand miles away in autumn's grief, forever a stranger;\nA lifetime of sickness, ascending this terrace alone.\nHardship and bitter regret have thickened my frosted temples;
Down and out, I have just now stopped my cup of turbid wine."}

