{"translation":"The wind is swift, the sky vast, apes wail in sorrow;
Islets clear, sands white, birds wheel and return.
Endless falling leaves rustle down in sorrow;
Unending Yangtze rolls on in ceaseless flow.
A thousand miles of autumn grief, a constant wanderer;
A hundred years of illness, alone I climb this height.
Hardship and bitter regret have silvered my temples;
In poverty and decline, I’ve just put down my wine cup."}

