The wind is swift, the sky high, apes wail mournfully;  
Islands clear, sands white, birds wheel and return.  
Endless falling leaves rustle down in autumn's sigh,  
The endless Yangtze roars on, ceaselessly rolling.  

A thousand miles of sorrow in autumn, I wander as a guest;  
A hundred years of illness, I climb this platform alone.  
Hardship and grief have turned my temples to frost;  
In poverty, I’ve just put down my cup of turbid wine.

