{"translation":"A new verse sung, a cup of wine—
Same weather as last year, the old pavilion.
Westward the sun descends—when will it return?
Helpless, the falling flowers drift away;
Like long-lost friends, swallows come back again.
Alone I wander the fragrant garden path."}

{"translation":"A new verse sung, a cup of wine—
