{"translation":"A new verse sung, a cup of wine—
Same weather as last year, the old pavilion.
When will the westward sun return?
Helplessly, flowers fall;
Like spirits long remembered, swallows come again.
Alone I tread the scented walk in the bower."}

{"translation":"I dwell at Yangtze's source, you at its end, 
Each day I think of you, yet see you not; 
We drink the same river’s water, friend. 
How long this flow? How long this grief? 
May your heart be like mine—sure and true— 
And never break the love we pursue."}

