message.content:
When the nation fell, mountains and rivers remain;  
In spring, the city is deep with grass and trees.  
Moved by the times, flowers shed tears;  
Hating parting, birds' cries pierce the heart.  
For three months, war flames have burned without cease;  
A letter from home is worth ten thousand in gold.  
White hair, scratched more and more, grows even thinner—  
So thin, it nearly cannot hold a hairpin.

