message.content:
The wind is swift, the sky high, apes wail mournfully;  
On clear islets, white sands, birds wheel and return.  
Endless fallen leaves rustle down in drifts,  
The endless Yangtze roars on, surging forward.  
A thousand miles of sorrow in autumn, I'm ever a traveler;  
In life's long span, plagued by illness, I climb this tower alone.  
Hardship and bitterness have whitened my temples with frost;  
Now, in decline, I've just laid down my cup of turbid wine.

