message.content:
The wind is swift, the sky high—apes wail mournfully;  
Islets clear, sands white—the birds wheel and return.  
Endless falling leaves rustle down in sighs;  
The endless Yangtze rolls on without rest.  
A thousand miles of sorrow in autumn, I wander as a guest;  
In life’s long span, sick and solitary, I climb this height.  
Hardship and bitter regret have silvered my temples with frost;  
Now broken, I’ve stopped drinking my coarse wine cup.

