message.content:
The wind is swift, the sky vast, apes wail mournfully;  
Islets clear, sands white, birds wheel and return.  
Endless falling leaves rustle down in autumn's sigh,  
The endless Yangtze roars on, ceaselessly rolling.  

A thousand miles of sorrow in autumn, I'm ever a traveler;  
A hundred years of illness, I stand alone on this terrace.  
Hardship and bitterness have whitened my temples with frost;  
In poverty, I've just laid down my cup of muddy wine.

