The city springs, where grass and weeds grow rank.
Moved by the times, the flowers splash my tears;
Hating our parting, birds startle my heart.
Beacon fires have burned three months on end;
A letter from my kin would be worth a fortune.
I scratch my white hair, growing ever sparser,
Till it can barely hold a hairpin.

