{
  "translation": "Before my bed, a pool of moonlight bright,\nI mistake it for frost on the ground.\nI lift my head to gaze at the radiant moon,\nThen lower it, thinking of my distant home.",
  "correspondence": [
    {
      "original": "床前明月光",
      "translation": "Before my bed, a pool of moonlight bright",
      "basis": "床译为bed，取常见义。“明月光”意译为moonlight bright，保留意象。"
    },
    {
      "original": "疑是地上霜",
      "translation": "I mistake it for frost on the ground",
      "basis": "疑译为mistake…for，取“恍惚觉得”之意，避免怀疑的歧义。"
    },
    {
      "original": "举头望明月",
      "translation": "I lift my head to gaze at the radiant moon",
      "basis": "举头译为lift my head，望译为gaze at，明月为the moon。radiant为增补修饰。"
    },
    {
      "original": "低头思故乡",
      "translation": "Then lower it, thinking of my distant home",
      "basis": "低头译为lower it（指头），思译为thinking of，故乡为my distant home。distant为增补修饰。"
    }
  ]
}

{"translation":"Climbing High

The wind is sharp, the sky so high, gibbons wail their mournful cry;
The isle is clear, the sand is white, birds wheel about in flight.
Boundless, the falling leaves come rustling down;
Endless, the Yangtze rolls on with a thunderous sound.
A thousand miles away, in autumn grief I’ve long been a stranger;
All my life, beset by ills, I climb this terrace all alone.
Times are hard and my troubles have thickened the frost at my temples;
Worn and spent, I’ve lately put down my cup of turbid wine."}

{
"translation": "I live at the source of the Yangtze,
You live at its mouth.
Day after day I long for you yet see you not—
We share the same river water.

When shall this water cease its flow?
When shall these parting sorrows end?
I only ask your heart to be as mine;
I shall not betray the love I bear."
}

{"translation":"Spring Lingers at Wuling

The wind has died, the dust is fragrant, the flowers are gone; 
It is late, and I am too weary to comb my hair. 
Things remain, but people are gone—everything has come to naught; 
I would speak, but tears flow first. 

I hear the spring at Twin Creeks is still fair, 
And half-consider taking a light boat there. 
But I fear the tiny sampan on Twin Creeks 
Cannot carry so much sorrow."}

{"translation":"A Morning Farewell at Wei City

The morning rain in Wei City has settled the light dust;
The inn is green, the willows fresh in their hue.
I urge you to drink another cup of wine—
West of Yang Pass, you'll find no old friends with you."}

{
"translation": "I live at the head of the Yangtze, you live at its tail.
Every day I long for you yet cannot see you, though we share the waters of the Yangtze.
When will this water cease? When will this longing end?
I only wish your heart were like mine — then I would never fail this love of ours."
}

