A thousand miles away, I grieve for autumn, forever a sojourner;\nA hundred years of life, yet mostly ill, I climb this terrace alone.
Hardships and bitter regrets have thickened the frost upon my temples;
Sunk in despair, I lately have set down my cup of turbid wine."}

