message.content:
{"translation":"A new song sung, a cup of wine drained,
The same old pavilion, the weather as last year's.
Westward the setting sun descends—when will it return?

Helplessly, the blossoms fall and go;
Seemingly familiar, the swallows come again.
On the fragrant path of this small garden, I pace alone."}

messages.content:
A song of new words, a cup of wine;
The same old pavilion, same weather as last year.
When will the setting sun return?

Helplessly, the flowers fall away;
Familiar, the swallows come again.
I pace alone on the fragrant path of my small garden.

