The isle is clear, the sand is white, birds wheel in flight.
Boundless, the falling leaves descend with rustling sound;
Endless, the Yangtze’s waves come rolling down in might.
Ten thousand miles away, I grieve for autumn, ever roaming;
A hundred years of illness, I climb this terrace alone.
Hardship and bitter regret have thickened my frosty hair;
Down and out, I’ve just had to stop my cup of cloudy wine.

