message.content:
The nation is broken, hills and streams remain;
Spring in the city, grass and trees grow deep.
Moved by the times, flowers draw my tears;
Hating parting, birds alarm my heart.
Beacon fires have burned for three months;
A letter from home is worth ten thousand in gold.
I scratch my white hair, it grows ever sparser,
So thin it can scarce hold the hairpin.

