message.content:
Autumn Evening in the Mountain

New-washed, the empty mountain brims with air;
The evening deepens, autumn everywhere.
The bright moon glows through gaps among the pines;
A clear spring ripples over stony lines.
Bamboo rustles—washer-girls returning home;
Lotus leaves stir—a fishing skiff drifts down.
Let spring’s fragrant blooms fade as they will—
Here the wandering prince may linger still.

