译文：The wind is sharp, the sky is high, the gibbons cry their sorrow;
The islet is clear, the sand is white, the birds wheel round and round.
Boundless, the falling leaves come rustling down;
Endless, the Yangtze rolls its waters toward me.
Ten thousand miles away, I mourn the autumn, ever a stranger;
A hundred years of illness, I climb this terrace alone.
Hardship and bitter regret have thickened my frosty temples;
In my wretchedness, I have just now laid down my cup of turbid wine.

