译文：After fresh rain in empty hills, the evening air turns autumn chill.
Bright moonlight filters through the pines;
Clear spring water slips over stones.
Bamboo rustles as washerwomen return;
Lotus leaves stir as fishing boats slip by.
Let spring’s blossoms fade as they will —
Here a prince may well choose to stay.

