{"translation":"Spring Prospect

The nation is shattered, yet mountains and rivers remain;
In spring the city brims with grass and trees grown wild.
Moved by the times, flowers draw tears;
Grieving at parting, birds startle the heart.
Beacon fires have burned for three months straight—
A single family letter would be worth its weight in gold.
I scratch my whitening hair, which thins evermore,
Barely long enough now to hold a hairpin."}

{"translation":"Seeing Off Meng Haoran at Yellow Crane Tower

My old friend bids farewell to the west at Yellow Crane Tower,
Amid the misty blossoms of March he goes down to Yangzhou.
His lone sail, a distant shadow, vanishes into the blue emptiness;
I see only the Yangtze River flowing to the horizon."}

