{"translation":"Huanxisha: A New Lyric Sung, a Cup of Wine Held

A new lyric sung, a cup of wine held; 
The weather same as last year, the pavilion old.
The sun sets in the west—when will it return?

Helplessly, the blossoms fall away; 
Seemingly familiar, the swallows return.
On the fragrant path of the small garden, I pace alone."}

{"translation":"A New Song Sung, a Cup of Wine in Hand

A new song sung, a cup of wine in hand;
Last year's weather, the old pavilions' stand.
As the sun sets in the west, when will it return?

Helplessly, the flowers fall away;
Seemingly familiar, the swallows return.
On the fragrant path of the small garden, I pace alone, lingering."}

