The wind has fallen, the dust is fragrant, flowers are done;
Late in the day, too weary to comb my hair.
Things remain, the person is gone, all is at an end;
Wanting to speak, tears flow first.

I hear the Twin Streams are still fair in spring;
I think of drifting a light boat there.
But I fear the little boats of the Twin Streams
Cannot carry so heavy a load of sorrow.

