message.content:
{"translation":"Night sees off a guest at Xunyang River head;
Maple leaves and reed flowers shiver in autumn dread.
The host dismounts while the guest steps aboard;
They raise their cups, but no music to accord.
Drunk, joy fades; parting is grim and bare;
Into the vast river moonlight seems to stare.
Suddenly, pipa music drifts from the water;
The host forgets to leave, the guest delays his border.
Seeking the sound, softly they ask who plays;
The music stops, she hesitates to say her ways.
They move their boat near and invite her face to face;
More wine is brought, lamps relit, the feast takes place.
