译文：The wind is sharp, the sky is high, the gibbons cry with grief,
The isles are clear, the sands are white, the birds wheel back.

Boundless, the falling leaves come rustling down;
Endless, the great river rolls before me on its way.

Ten thousand miles away, grieving at autumn, I am always a stranger;
A hundred years of sickness, I climb this terrace alone.

