message.content:
{"translation":"A new song sung, a cup of wine,
Same weather, same old pavilion.
When will the setting sun return?
The falling flowers, helpless, gone;
The swallows, vaguely known.
Alone I pace the fragrant path."}

Ten years, life and death, both vast and dim;
Not brooding, yet impossible to forget.

A lone grave a thousand miles away;
Nowhere to speak of this desolation.

Even if we met, you would not know me—
Dust fills my face, temples like frost.

Last night in a quiet dream I returned to our home;
By the small window, you were dressing your hair.

We looked at each other, speechless;
Only tears, a thousand lines.

I know where my heart will break year after year:
The bright moonlit night, the hill of short pines.

{"translation":"The wind has stilled, the dust is fragrant, the flowers are all gone;
The day grows late; too weary to comb my hair.
The things remain, the people are gone, all things are done;
I wish to speak, but first the tears flow.

I hear they say the spring at Shuangxi is still fair,
I too had thought of drifting in a light boat.
I only fear the zemeng boats upon Shuangxi
Cannot carry so much sorrow."}

