message.content:
{"translation":"The wind is sharp, the sky is high, apes' cries wail;
The isle is clear, the sand is white, birds wheel in flight.
Boundless, the falling leaves descend with rustling sound;
Endless, the Yangtze rolls on, roaring down in might.
Ten thousand miles away, I grieve for autumn, ever roaming;
A hundred years of illness, I climb the height alone.
Hardship and bitter regret have thickened my frosty hair;
Down and out, I've just had to stop my cup of dregs of wine."}

The wind is keen, the sky is high, apes cry their woe;
The islet clear, the sand white, birds wheel and go.
Boundless the falling leaves rustle adown;
Endless the rolling river surges along.
Ten thousand miles I drift in autumn, a guest;
A hundred years, full of illness, I climb the terrace alone.
Hardship and bitter regret have thickened my frosted temples;
Spent, I have newly ceased my cup of turbid wine.

