{"translation":"When the nation fell, mountains and rivers remain;
In spring, the city is deep in grass and trees.
Moved by the times, flowers shed tears;
Hating parting, birds alarm the heart.
War beacons burn for three long months—
A letter from home is worth ten thousand in gold.
I scratch my white hair, now even shorter,
So thin it nearly cannot hold a hairpin."}
